 non-executable, untagged executable, or no evidence. It returns the sorted union of tagged test files, lists a tagged test case's non-test evidence and declared non-executable evidence without running it, and returns every gap: a system requirement that no scoped test case verifies, directly or through a scoped low-level requirement, or a low-level requirement that no scoped test case verifies, an untagged executable test case, or a test case with no evidence; sibling low-level requirements are included. Code-touching is a changed path from merge base to staged tree under the declared source or tests roots, with both ends of a rename counted; all other paths are not code-touching. A code-touching row with no requirement reference refuses by name; one with any gap refuses partial naming every gap; one with no tagged file and no gap refuses empty; a row not touching code reports gaps without refusal, permits an empty set, and runs a non-empty set. Missing or multiple claims, malformed frontmatter or requirement references, a missing referenced system requirement, unreadable or malformed registries, paths declaration, trunk declaration, or a test-declaration refusal refuse by name; an unreadable input outranks partial and empty. The derivation reads the lane's own tree and never widens to the whole bar. Its covered behavior is the claim copy, scope walk, classes, changed-path decision, input refusals, set printing, attestation, draw, rendering, and closed-lane routes; hand-edited claim copies or records, path aliases, and sub-second timing windows are outside this bound.\""," rationale = \"One closed derivation prevents recording, drawing, and rendering from disagreeing about required verification while preserving named, repairable refusals.\""," test_refs = \"TC-413; TC-414; TC-415; TC-416; TC-417; TC-418; TC-419; TC-420\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-995\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":4106,"oldLines":7,"newStart":4106,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"The walk includes all scoped test cases, classifies each once, returns sorted tagged files and listed non-test evidence, and reports no gap for a directly verified system requirement.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_a_drafted_tc_is_in_scope; tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_a_tagged_tc_lists_its_non_test_evidence_beside_the_set; tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_a_tc_falls_in_exactly_one_class; tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_an_llr_naming_two_srs_is_reached_from_either; tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_an_sr_verified_only_directly_has_no_gap; tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_the_set_is_the_sorted_files_of_the_tagged_nodes; tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_the_walk_unions_direct_tcs_and_tcs_through_the_llrs\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-414]"]},{"oldStart":4117,"oldLines":7,"newStart":4117,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"Every required gap is named; a system requirement verified only through its low-level requirement has no gap; partial outranks empty; and empty applies only when no tagged file and no gap exist.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_review_set.py::test_empty_is_refused_only_with_no_gap_and_no_tagged_file; tests/test_review_set.py::test_partial_names_every_gap_and_outranks_empty; tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_an_sr_verified_only_through_its_llr_has_no_gap; tests/test_review_set_walk.py::test_each_gap_is_named\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-415]"]},{"oldStart":4128,"oldLines":7,"newStart":4128,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"Declared source or tests paths, including both sides of a rename, are code-touching; a code-touching row without a requirement reference refuses by name, and a non-code row permits an empty set and reports gaps.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_review_set.py::test_a_code_touching_row_naming_no_sr_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_review_set.py::test_a_rename_out_of_src_still_touches_code; tests/test_review_set.py::test_a_row_touching_no_code_and_naming_no_sr_is_an_empty_set; tests/test_review_set.py::test_a_src_or_tests_change_is_code_touching_and_any_other_path_is_not; tests/test_review_set.py::test_empty_is_refused_only_with_no_gap_and_no_tagged_file; tests/test_review_set.py::test_gaps_on_a_row_touching_no_code_are_reported_never_refused; tests/test_review_set.py::test_partial_names_every_gap_and_outranks_empty; tests/test_review_set.py::test_the_changed_paths_are_counted_from_the_merge_base\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-416]"]},{"oldStart":4139,"oldLines":7,"newStart":4139,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"Malformed or unreadable inputs and a tag-reader refusal refuse by name; and a closed lane reads its closed work-item copy.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_review_set.py::test_a_lane_closed_in_its_own_tree_reads_its_closed_copy; tests/test_review_set.py::test_each_unreadable_input_refuses_by_name; tests/test_review_set.py::test_the_tag_readers_refusal_passes_through\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-417]"]},{"oldStart":4150,"oldLines":7,"newStart":4150,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"Attestation accepts no hand test list, derives before any bar, preserves branch and index and runs no bar on refusal, runs the review bar then derived files, records their digest, and prints the result.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_integrate_attest.py::test_a_derivation_refusal_runs_no_bar_and_leaves_branch_and_index; tests/test_integrate_attest.py::test_a_row_touching_no_code_runs_the_bar_alone; tests/test_integrate_attest.py::test_attest_prints_the_gaps_a_row_touching_no_code_reports; tests/test_integrate_atte